+/*
+ * S-R mode engine (WP2-DESIGN §3.4 step 0, §4.3-§4.7, §5.2-§5.4, §6): the
+ * PPE's one chip-wide mode around the register sequences of ppe_sr_seq.c.
+ * It keeps the generation every offer is judged under, the dirty marks of
+ * topology events, the hook that turns any degraded latch into FAULT, the
+ * counters, the scope and the deadline arithmetic.
+ *
+ * Pure, like the sequences: ppe_sr.c binds it to the kernel (the offload
+ * lock, RTNL, RCU, the conduit's reference, the rtl8_4s state word, regmap,
+ * works and notifiers), and a desk harness drives it on a mock. Every
+ * function taking a struct ppe_sr_eng runs under the offload lock
+ * (priv->lock), but ppe_sr_eng_gen(), ppe_sr_eng_state() and
+ * ppe_sr_eng_ticket(), which are lockless.
+ */
